::ingredients

(veal cutlet) 4, ~150g each
(egg) 2
(lemon) 1
(flour) 100g
(bread crumbs) 150g
(frying fat) = (butter) 100g -OR- (butter, clarified) 100g
# Method-only seasoning
(salt) as needed
(paprika) as needed
(pepper) as needed

::equipment

(bowl, for flour)
(bowl, for egg)
(bowl, for crumbs)
(kitchen roll)
(board)
(meat tenderizer) -OR- (rolling pin)
(pan, deep)

::instructions

(flour) <place, in (bowl, for flour)>
(egg) <beat>
    <place, in (bowl, for egg)>
{seasoned crumbs} = (bread crumbs) + (salt) + (paprika)
    <place, in (bowl, for crumbs)>
(veal cutlet) <wash>
(veal cutlet) <dry, using (kitchen roll), gently>
(veal cutlet) <place, on (board)>
(veal cutlet) <beat, using (meat tenderizer) or using (rolling pin), to 0.5cm thick>
(veal cutlet) <season, with (salt) + (pepper), on both sides>
(veal cutlet) <coat, with (flour), in (bowl, for flour)>
(veal cutlet) <coat, with (egg), in (bowl, for egg)>
(veal cutlet) <coat, in (bowl, for crumbs), with the seasoned crumbs>
(frying fat) <melt, in (pan), not too hot; butter must not brown>
(veal cutlet) <fry, in (pan), each side; for example 3m per side> ?= golden brown on each side
    <serve, with (lemon), a piece>

::notes

The source prefers clarified butter over butter.
Beating the veal makes it tender.

::story

Original Austrian breaded meat, pan-fried in butter.

